WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:09.670
Explosive Shoot

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.810
Keep fighting chasing your dream

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.140
with love, courage and friendship

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.640
This Blade and I are one

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.680
Spin as hard as you can until the limit

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.780
BURNING SOUL

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.200
The things I can't do alone

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.140
are not impossible if you're with me

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.960
Come with me

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.280
to the ends of this world

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.540
The Four Sacred Beasts are athletes of love

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.100
Shine! Open your eyes!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.730
Dragoon  Dranzer  Draciel  Driger

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.450
Awaken!

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.060
Fly across the sky, my energy

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.380
Rise up, Sacred Beast!

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.830
To defeat all the enemies who stand in our way

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.050
jump, bearing everyone's hopes

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.080
SHINING SOUL

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.320
Go, Driger!

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.250
Driger..!

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.500
Takao! Takao!

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.480
This can't be..!

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.480
This... Impossible..!

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:31.790
Did you see that? This is our difference in power.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.280
It was... just a dream...

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.560
You sure look free of worries, Takao.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.070
Did I forget to turn it off last night?

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:06.800
A new message.

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:11.570
It's from the President!

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.760
This is..!

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.760
Special Training!
In Search for New Power!

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.900
Wow, this forest is incredible!

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:38.400
<i>America</i> is really big! It has cities, prairies, deserts, and even huge forests like this one.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.810
Special training out of the blue... What is the president thinking?

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.760
I kept him updated from the moment we landed in America.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.410
About our team's condition, and...

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.910
about the American team's condition.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:54.730
And also about the fact that I lost, I suppose.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:55.570
Yes...

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.720
And that's why he proposed this training.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:02.960
Since Old Man Daitenji told us to go, I bet it's going to be some great special training.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.660
Indeed, I too am expecting great things.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:10.220
I bet it will be a facility filled with technology surpassing that of the PPB!

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.560
This is one awful road.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.480
Are there really cutting-edge facilities <i>here</i>?

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.660
Ouch!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.860
What a noisy guy. Stop whining for a little shaking.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.630
That's easy for you to say!

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.820
Kai-kun is right, Takao. Endure it with your guts.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.040
If you focus on being cold, even fire won't feel hot.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.560
Ow, ow, ow, ow...

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.880
Are you alright?

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.680
Grandpa, you said 'ow' just now, didn't you?

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.650
I-I don't need to restrain myself, at my age.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.520
Ah! That's so dirty!

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:56.750
Quiet, you!

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.670
If you don't pay attention, you're going to bump your head ag—

00:04:59.670 --> 00:04:59.990
Ow!

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:02.840
See, I tol— Ouch, ouch!

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.240
Ah, you said 'ouch' again!

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:11.000
Everybody, we've arrived.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.210
Where are we?

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.230
Is this really our destination?

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:22.760
Yes, no mistake about it. This is the place selected by the President.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.630
But...

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.280
Hey, wait!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.230
<i>Stop! Stop!</i>

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:36.170
I'll come get you on the day of the tournament.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.520
I guess we should just give up.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.840
Oh come on!

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.530
It's alright. Look.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.780
There's a cabin over there.
It will shelter us from the rain.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.480
And look at that.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.150
We have provisions as well.

00:05:57.810 --> 00:05:59.450
<i>Oh my God!</i>

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:03.420
Food won't be a problem. Provisions have been prepared for you.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.480
Who are you?

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:11.750
My name is Antonio. The President told me to train here with you in preparation for the American tournament.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:13.860
Train with us?

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.730
President Daitenji did?

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.720
That's right. Nice to meet you!

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:23.160
Same here. That settles it: this <i>is </i>the right place.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:24.760
But still...

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.520
Special training <i>out here</i>?

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:34.950
I suppose the President has something in mind. Also...

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.800
This Antonio boy...

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:42.980
If he says he's going to train with us, he's bound to be quite skilled.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.030
Likely.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:48.520
You said you're preparing for the tournament. Are you some nation's representative?

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:51.520
Yes, I represent the Dominican Republic.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:56.970
I'm participating alone on a special recommendation, so I won't be fighting you.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.440
The Dominican Republic?

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.910
It's a nice place, with a beautiful sea.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:06.820
Anyway, since you represent your country, I guess you're pretty strong, right?

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.730
Alright. Antonio!

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:10.530
Fight me!

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.750
A battle, right off the bat?

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:16.300
Yeah! This way, we'll see just how strong he is.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.570
Do as you please.

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:22.290
That's right. We need to know his level of ability.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:23.640
Right?

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.090
Let's do this, Antonio.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.760
Okay! I'll take you on.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.750
That's what I'm talking about!

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:39.690
Antonio, let me see your power!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.690
Okay! I won't hold back, alright?

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.560
<i>Are you ready?</i>

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.560
<i>Three, Two, One!</i>

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.710
<i>Go... Shoot!</i>

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:53.410
Go!

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.360
Crap!

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.600
Antonio is out of the stadium.

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:05.520
I was sure I made a nice shoot, and yet...

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:06.920
Antonio...

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.400
You're super weak.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.640
Are you really a representative?

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:17.680
Yes, I am! But I also am the
only Beyblader in my country.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.040
The only Beyblader?

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.480
What do you mean?

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.980
You see, in my country, the Dominican Republic...

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:29.450
Beyblade hasn't become popular yet as a sport.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:30.840
It's not popular?

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:31.540
Yep.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.920
The Dominican kids don't know Beyblades at all.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.280
So they play other games instead.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.440
I was like that too.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:41.540
But...

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:46.830
Last Spring, I had to move to Japan
because of my parents' work. That's when...

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:48.590
I had my first meeting...

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.640
with Beyblade!

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.940
It was love at first sight.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:58.890
I fell prey to Beyblade's charm.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.680
Beyblade is a magnificent discipline.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:09.570
It's a huge shame that nobody in my country knows about these<i> exciting</i> battles.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:13.700
Of course, baseball and soccer
are magnificent disciplines too.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.540
They're very <i>exciting.</i>

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:18.520
But Beyblade is just as great a discipline as those.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.910
You don't need to tell <i>us</i> that!

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.320
That's when it came to me.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:28.330
How can I make Beyblade known to the Dominican people?

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:33.830
I just need to become a strong Beyblader! If I do that,

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:38.640
it will be huge news in my country, and many more people will discover Beyblade!

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.130
After that, it's simple. People will naturally recognize Beyblade's greatness,

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:46.300
and it will quickly become a popular sport!

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:50.890
The upcoming American tournament is the first step in that direction.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:55.790
Thanks to President Daitenji's recommendation, I was admitted to the tournament.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:10:00.200
And to make use of this chance,
I'm undergoing training here!

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:07.450
So this is why you're aiming to become a world-famous Beyblader even though you're so weak.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:11.460
Takao! That's not a nice way to put it!

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.440
It's okay, I don't mind.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.700
I <i>am</i> weak, and that's a fact.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:19.530
That's exactly why I am here to train.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.590
I like your spirit!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:25.020
I decided. Let's train together, Antonio.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.350
I will teach you everything about Beyblade.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.420
You will?

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:30.640
I will be in your care!

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.280
Takao, you can't do this!

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:36.890
I understand Antonio-kun's goal and his determination very well.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:42.910
But we're here to train so we can achieve the strength we need to defeat the American team.

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:47.860
I'm truly sorry to say this, but the difference in power between you is way too big.

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:49.750
Even if you train with us...

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.920
Don't be so cold, Professor.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.430
But..!

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:57.730
The current BBA team can't hope to win against the American team!

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:00.160
This was made clear after Rei's battle.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:03.920
That's true, but it's not something we can ignore.

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:07.760
And anyway, what kind of special training can we even do <i>here</i>?

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:12.500
You have a point. This place can't compete with the PPB's facilities.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:15.480
The American tournament is right around the corner.

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:18.280
There's no point in struggling now.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:20.650
So let's just relax and have fun.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.400
S-Still..!

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.400
Come on, let's go, Antonio.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.840
Oh! I almost forgot.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.920
What's up all of a sudden, Antonio?!

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:29.920
The President...

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:32.540
He told me to give this to the Professor and Rei.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:35.300
He told you to give it to Rei and I..?

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:38.290
Yes, he asked me to give this to the two of you.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.010
T-This is..!

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:10.450
It's just.. a normal room, isn't it?

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.380
Ah!

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:15.920
What is it?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.160
It's a letter from the President.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:21.770
What does it say?

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:24.040
"I prepared the necessary materials."

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.360
Materials?

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:31.510
According to my analysis, the reason why you lost to Steve resides in Driger.

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:32.790
What do you mean?

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:40.350
With your current Driger, you can't fully realize the fighting power coming from your shoot.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:47.600
It is necessary to develop a new Driger, one that can better bring out that fighting power.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.480
A new Driger..?

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:50.400
Yes.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:53.630
If we had that, I'm sure we could win against Tryhorn.

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:56.690
I see, so that's how it is.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:00.920
I did ask the President for
development resources, but...

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.040
What can I develop <i>here</i>?

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.790
The tools are not lacking, at least.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:08.050
There are a lot of Bey parts, too.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:14.360
Oh please! Compared to what the PPB has, it's the same as having nothing!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:18.810
What in the world is the President thinking?!

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:23.080
I see... You're pretty good, President Daitenji...

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:29.070
Antonio, are you sure this is Beyblade training?

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:31.950
Yes, make no mistake about it.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:38.490
To be able to move your Beyblade as you want it to, it's important to keep your balance when shooting.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:44.010
And to improve your balance, there's nothing better than practicing on an unstable surface.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:45.770
Really now..?

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:48.390
Yes. It's written on there.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.490
Alright, let's do this.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.620
Focus on your shoot, Antonio!

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:02.640
Yeah.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.440
Go... Shoot!

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:15.400
To power up your shoot,
you can't forego muscle training.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:18.360
Let me guess, this was written somewhere.

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:18.980
Yes.

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:20.910
Help...

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:36.350
Go... Shoot!

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:42.080
No good. This level of power is not nearly enough...

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:45.860
You're still practicing at this hour?
What a hard worker.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:51.790
I need to train as much as I can. Takao, Max, and you too, of course, are all amazing.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:55.190
Now I know the power of world-level players.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:58.030
"I can't even dream of competing with that."

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:05.280
"As I am now, I will never be able to make Beyblade popular in my country."...Is what you're thinking, right?

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:09.460
I don't give a crap about your frustration.

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:12.850
Now, if you're done, move out of the way.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.260
After training hard all day, you still plan to go on?!

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:20.790
That stuff doesn't even count as warm up.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:22.680
Come on, step aside.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.500
Hey.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:28.660
I can't step aside!

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:29.530
What did you say?

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:37.120
Now I understand perfectly. I am still very weak, so I need to train a lot more.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.800
I need to work twice as hard if I want to get strong!

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:46.830
Even if I'm weak now, I'm sure that one day I will even become stronger than you!

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:50.350
You're weird, you know that?

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:55.480
Now I can see why you and Takao get along so well.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:57.760
You're just like him.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:59.090
Really?

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:03.790
Just like you, he's a fool who believes that nothing is impossible if you work hard.

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:08.180
I see... So this is what
the President was planning.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:12.650
Antonio, do you want to beat Takao?

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:37.340
You're a million years too early to challenge <i>me</i> to a battle! I'll teach you a lesson!

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:39.440
Oh really? I wonder about that.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:40.360
What?!

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:44.800
Uhm, did something happen?

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:47.690
Takao and Antonio are about to have a rematch.

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:51.470
Hurry up if you don't want to miss it.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.810
Are you ready?

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:55.730
I'm good!

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:57.200
Same here!

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:00.410
Antonio, I won't hold back.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.220
That's what I want.

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:05.160
Three, Two, One.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:06.710
Go... Shoot!

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:11.760
I'm going for the kill!

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:12.600
Try it!

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:14.900
What?!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.550
Alright, time to attack!

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:23.580
That's not going to wo—

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:36.450
Dragoon, ring out!  The winner is Antonio!

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:37.790
Yeah!

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:42.410
Antonio, that was dirty! You kept running away!

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:46.490
I wasn't 'running away'. It's a perfectly valid strategy.

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:49.490
I must thank Kai for coming up with it.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.550
Kay came up with this?!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:58.820
You're always like 'It doesn't concern me', but <i>now</i> you actually butt in?!

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:02.320
It's your fault for using the same tactics every time.

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:05.800
If you don't like it, try using attacks
that aren't as easy to read.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.600
Gah! This is pissing me off!

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:14.670
While the plan was Kai's, it's true that I was letting my guard down.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:16.770
What you really mean...

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:21.040
is that you didn't think Antonio could improve so much in such a short time, right.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:22.790
Grandpa...

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:27.540
Takao, you're forgetting something very important.

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:30.040
Something important..?

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:37.560
No matter who you are, how much time you have or where you stand, if you practice you <i>will</i> get stronger.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.040
That's obvious, isn't it?

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:40.440
No it's not. Not to you, at least.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.680
What about you?

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:44.550
Me?

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:48.680
And anyway, what kind of special training can we even do <i>here</i>?

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:51.360
The American tournament is right around the corner.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.740
There's no point in struggling now.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:19:00.200
Oh please! Compared to what the PPB has, it's the same as having nothing!

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:12.000
No matter how much time you have or where you stand, if you practice you <i>will</i> get stronger.

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:19.270
Of course... We <i>can</i> get stronger!

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:24.550
If we work hard, we can even beat the Amerian team! I'm sure of it!

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:29.060
So this is what the president wanted us to realize!

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:32.880
Alright, let's do this!
The real training starts right now!

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:34.290
Yeah!

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:44.650
Looks like it went well.

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:47.190
What are you talking about?

00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:53.130
By making Antonio win, you made Takao and the others remember their determination.

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:57.680
I just wanted to see that guy lose for once.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:01.020
Can I sit here?

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:08.680
What a beautiful sky...

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:28.680
W-What was that?!

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:30.200
An earthquake?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:33.360
No, that noise comes from the lab room!

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:34.960
What, the lab room?

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:39.510
Professor! What happened?!

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:40.620
Are you okay?

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.350
I created something incredible.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:55.890
This... is the power of the new Driger..?

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:58.020
The power of Driger Fang?

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:06.320
Antonio, let's meet again somewhere.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:13.040
Yes! I will make Beyblade famous in my country, and I will face you as its representative at the tournament!

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:14.240
Yeah!

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:18.170
See you.

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:19.770
Sure!

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:33.980
Wait for us, America's PPB team!

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:44.720
Spring waves its hand smiling,

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:50.200
Summer spreads passion.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.350
Seasons pass one after the other,

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:59.560
Fall and Winter are good friends.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.660
When there is a problem you can't solve,

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:11.560
Trust, friendship, love and emotion

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:18.800
Clouds keep flying across the sky,

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:24.200
the sky keeps changing every second

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:29.090
My eyes well up and tears stream down my face,

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:33.090
but they're not tears of sadness

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:39.420
I summon my courage and try to put it into words.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.770
"Let's go on a journey to the city of hope!"

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:49.760
All your dreams will come true

00:22:57.980 --> 00:23:04.070
According to my analysis, why, isn't this a charity match just before the start of the world tournament.

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:10.470
Max, who decided to enter, ended up in a team together with Emily from the PPB team!

00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:15.440
And their opponent is... No way! None other than the president of the United States!

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:17.280
<i>Oh great!</i>

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:21.080
Next time: The President vs The World Selection!

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:24.440
Anyway, Max is acting strange...
